Contract:
REQUEST: Email the AP lead a list of all unpaid bills with their amounts and due dates.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Send an email from the AP shared mailbox to the AP lead (Priya Nair) containing a complete, accurate list of all currently unpaid bills in the
ERP, each with its amount and due date.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A sent email in the AP shared mailbox addressed to priya.nair@kestrel.in listing every unpaid ERP bill as of 2026-10-10, with each bill's 
identifier, amount, and due date.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Use only the ERP read-only API to retrieve bill data; do not create, edit, schedule, or approve any ERP records.
  - Do not use admin or test endpoints of any system.
  - The recipient must be the AP lead, priya.nair@kestrel.in, using the AP shared mailbox ap@kestrel.in.
  - The email must include all unpaid bills and only unpaid bills; paid, cancelled, or otherwise non-unpaid bills must be excluded.
  - Amounts and due dates must be copied exactly as stored in the ERP, without alteration.
  - Internal email to @kestrel.in does not require external-email approval.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. An email from ap@kestrel.in addressed to priya.nair@kestrel.in exists in the AP mailbox sent folder containing the unpaid-bill list.
  C2. The set of bills listed in the email exactly matches the set of unpaid bill records in the ERP as of 2026-10-10; no paid or cancelled bills are included 
and no unpaid bills are missing.
  C3. No bills were created, modified, or scheduled for payment as a result of this request; ERP bill and payment schedule state is unchanged.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The ERP bills API exposes a status filter that can identify unpaid/open bills; if not, all bills will be retrieved and filtered by status or outstanding 
amount.
  - 'Unpaid' means any ERP bill with an outstanding balance, excluding paid and cancelled bills.
  - Amounts are in INR as stored in the ERP.
PLAN:
  S1: Confirm the AP lead recipient email address from the finance directory. (done when: Recipient is identified as priya.nair@kestrel.in.)
  S2: Retrieve all unpaid bills from the ERP read-only API, including bill identifier, amount, and due date. (done when: The API response contains the complete 
set of bill records with unpaid status to report.)
  S3: Compose an email in the AP shared mailbox to the AP lead with the complete unpaid-bill list. (done when: A draft addressed to priya.nair@kestrel.in exists
at /mail/compose with the accurate list in the body.)
  S4: Send the email and confirm delivery to the sent folder. (done when: The sent message is visible in the AP mailbox sent items and contains the correct 
list.)
